# Hard Rules Verification Checklist

Before marking ANY task as verified/complete, you MUST have a checklist entry
for each of the following. If ANY box is unchecked, the task is NOT done.

## Pre-verification checklist (run this EVERY time)

```
[ ] 1. Enumerated ALL requirements of the task (written out, not just remembered)
[ ] 2. Built/updated an ISOLATED test scene (dedicated .tscn + .gd, no main scene)
[ ] 3. Captured BEFORE screenshot (pre-change state, isolated world)
       - If the change is already applied: temporarily revert, capture, re-apply
[ ] 4. Captured AFTER screenshot (post-change state, isolated world)
[ ] 5. Compared before/after — delta is visible and matches the requirement
[ ] 6. Read EVERY screenshot with the Read tool and described what is ACTUALLY shown
[ ] 7. Ran the test in the FULL game (main scene or FFA) and captured in-game screenshot
[ ] 8. Report JSON verdict is PASS / expected fields match
[ ] 9. Screenshots + report JSON are committed to git (git add tools/selftest/results/)
[ ] 10. App restarted with tools/restart_app.ps1 so the user sees the change live
```

## How to use

1. Before starting a task, copy the checklist into your todo list.
2. Tick each box as you complete it.
3. If you cannot tick a box, the task is NOT done — note what is missing.
4. **Never** mark a task "verified" or "complete" in PLAN.md with any box unchecked.
5. **Never** skip the BEFORE screenshot. If you already made the code change,
   you MUST temporarily revert to capture the before state.
6. **Never** rely on the report JSON alone — you must open each PNG with the
   Read tool and describe what you see.
7. **Never** leave screenshots uncommitted. Run `git add tools/selftest/results/`
   and commit + push after every verification batch.

## Common mistakes to avoid

- Marking a task done based on "the report says PASS" without reading the screenshots.
- Skipping the isolated test and going straight to the full game.
- Capturing only an "after" screenshot without a "before" for comparison.
- Forgetting to commit the result PNGs and report JSON to git.
- Not restarting the app at the end of the turn.
- Using a single screenshot to "verify" a multi-phase feature.
